{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1550379-titans-without-gods-gods-without-titans","id":1550379,"title":"Titans without Gods, Gods without Titans.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-25T06:30:09-07:00","id":1550379,"title":"Titans without Gods, Gods without Titans.","content":"This is about a question. Since these beings have been around for awhile, and we know that Pantheons have been destroyed or shattered with a few random survivors, are there groups of Titan that have eliminated or conquered their Gods? <br /> <br /> The Lovecraft mythos might be a fine candidate for Titans that erased or conquered their Gods. <br /> <br /> There also should be Pantheons that killed off or conquered their Titans. Since we know that Odin killed Ymir, ending the Ice Age, the Titans can be beaten. Maybe they can sometimes be tamed or reformed. <br /> <br /> Still what does this board think about these things?<br /> <br /> Are there any candidates for a Pantheon of Titans without Gods, other than Lovecraft's crew?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T06:05:52-07:00","id":1550787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1550379-titans-without-gods-gods-without-titans#post1550379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lovecraft mythos might be a fine candidate for Titans that erased or conquered their Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember correctly, Masks of the Mythos makes it clear that the Great Old Ones aren't Titans, or even really &quot;Gods&quot; as commonly understood. They don't have access to Titanic Callings to begin with, but instead are defined by their own set of Mythos-exclusive Callings; some share names with Titanic Callings, but they're otherwise treated are completely distinct. The GOOs also have <i>Awareness</i> rather than <i>Legend</i>, and even their Fate doesn't work the same way.<br /> My point is, the Mythos are an &quot;outside context problem&quot; for The World. They operate according to their own set of rules, and so the traditional God/Titan duality doesn't really apply to them \u2014 a duality which, mind you, is already stated in-universe to be a largely engineered social construct defined more by cultural posturing and theopolitics than anything else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1550379-titans-without-gods-gods-without-titans#post1550379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There also should be Pantheons that killed off or conquered their Titans. Since we know that Odin killed Ymir, ending the Ice Age, the Titans can be beaten. Maybe they can sometimes be tamed or reformed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's already the Sh\u00e9n's established policy regarding Titans: absorbing them into the Celestial Bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1550379-titans-without-gods-gods-without-titans#post1550379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any candidates for a Pantheon of Titans without Gods, other than Lovecraft's crew?</div> </div> </div> </div>The closest thing in existing canon to a Titan-dominated Pantheon is the Atua; in their original entry in Demigod, 6 out of the 8 Atua listed have at least one Titanic Calling, although it's largely a result of the Atua rejecting the entire God/Titan duality entirely.<br /> As for what you're thinking about, I don't think any existing IRL mythology can fit the mold. Titans in Scion are meant to represent the designated &quot;antagonists&quot; of IRL mythologies. A Pantheon where the Titans won would require a mythology where the &quot;protagonists&quot; (Gods and Heroes) never win, and what kind of IRL human culture would not only consistently tell itself stories like that, but also build an entire belief system around them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T14:43:21-07:00","id":1550815,"title":"","content":"Possibly a mentally ill one.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, since dead or lost pantheons are associated with dead or lost cultures, perhaps the culture died and other nearby cultures took over their gods and titans to be the Titans of their pantheon.<br /> <br /> Look at &quot;Yam,&quot; a titan of the Canaanite pantheon. Yam is the Titan of the wilderness and wastes, both the sea and the desert.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 05-07-2025, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-17T23:26:24-08:00","id":1557719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1550379-titans-without-gods-gods-without-titans#post1550379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is about a question. Since these beings have been around for awhile, and we know that Pantheons have been destroyed or shattered with a few random survivors, are there groups of Titan that have eliminated or conquered their Gods?<br /> <br /> The Lovecraft mythos might be a fine candidate for Titans that erased or conquered their Gods.<br /> <br /> There also should be Pantheons that killed off or conquered their Titans. Since we know that Odin killed Ymir, ending the Ice Age, the Titans can be beaten. Maybe they can sometimes be tamed or reformed.<br /> <br /> Still what does this board think about these things?<br /> <br /> Are there any candidates for a Pantheon of Titans without Gods, other than Lovecraft's crew?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't call the entities from Lovecraft mythos Titans. Rather, they serve as a nihilistic take on the powers that be.<br /> <br /> Basically, the mythos presents us with the question of <i>&quot;what if the gods were just completely disconnected from us?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> In the mind of Lovecraft, the only appropriate response to such a universe would be to go insane, since nothing actually matters.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------------<br /> <br /> But to address the question, immortals don't die easily. Especially not when it comes to religions that feature reincarnation.<br /> <br /> Titanomachy reveals that <b>Ymir</b> is still alive, because his daughter / granddaughter took on his mantle and allowed him to be reborn in her body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}